  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Federal contract obligations for NAICS 334511 total $10.4B in FY2026 to date. There were 6,204 awards and the average award size was $1.7M. Obligations are down 43.4% year over year. Obligations peaked in FY25 at $18.4B and then moved to $10.4B in FY26. Earlier fiscal-year totals were $13.2B in FY21, $13.9B in FY22, $17B in FY23, and $17.1B in FY24. The Department of Defense accounted for the largest share of FY2026 to date obligations at $8.4B, followed by the Department of Transportation at $1B and the Department of Homeland Security at $818M. A small group of prime contractors captured the largest FY2026 to date awards, led by RAYTHEON COMPANY at $1.6B and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $725M. These figures are contract obligations and FY2026 totals are partial because they reflect fiscal year to date activity.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What changed year over year?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 43.4% year over year. After rising from $13.2B in FY21 to $18.4B in FY25, obligations moved to $10.4B in FY26. The drop shows a sharp reduction in FY2026 to date compared with the prior year level of $18.4B."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the biggest buyers and sellers in FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buyer at $8.4B, followed by the Department of Transportation at $1B and the Department of Homeland Security at $818M. Top vendors include RAYTHEON COMPANY at $1.6B and LOCKHEED MARTIN CORPORATION at $725M, with other large awards to vendors such as NORTHROP GRUMMAN SYSTEMS CORPORATION and INDRA AIR TRAFFIC, INC."
      }
